<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a self-contained review of the three self-distillation based objective functions introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
These extend upon the original distillation-based objectives introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
To this end, we first recall three key properties of the flow map.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5</span></span><span id="Thmproposition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Flow map characterization)<span id="Thmproposition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}{x}_{t}=v_{t}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}{x}_{t}=v_{t}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> denote a probability flow ODE, and let <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}:[0,1]^{2}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}:[0,1]^{2}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its flow map.
Then,</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the unique solution to the Lagrangian equation,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x))\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.220em">∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x))\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the unique solution to the Eulerian equation,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x)+\nabla X_{s,t}(x)b_{s}(x)=0\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.220em">∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x)+\nabla X_{s,t}(x)b_{s}(x)=0\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">iii.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies the semigroup condition,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)=X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,u,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.220em">∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)=X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))\qquad\forall\&gt;(x,s,u,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We simply prove the forward direction: that the flow map satisfies each property.
The proof of uniqueness follows similarly and can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each property follows from the defining condition</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x_{s})=x_{t}\qquad\forall\&gt;(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.220em">∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x_{s})=x_{t}\qquad\forall\&gt;(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the derivative with respect to time, we find that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\partial_{t}x_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\partial_{t}x_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{t}(x_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{t}(x_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is the Lagrangian equation.
Noting that <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the total derivative of equation <a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> with respect to <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we find</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})+\nabla X_{s,t}(x_{s})\partial_{t}{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})+\nabla X_{s,t}(x_{s})\partial_{t}{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})+\nabla X_{s,t}(x_{s})b_{s}(x_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})+\nabla X_{s,t}(x_{s})b_{s}(x_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Again, noting that <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The semigroup condition follows simply by noting that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x_{s}))=X_{u,t}(x_{u})=x_{t}=X_{s,t}(x_{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x_{s}))=X_{u,t}(x_{u})=x_{t}=X_{s,t}(x_{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in the main text, from the Lagrangian condition in equation <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Item i. ‣ Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we may observe that</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\lim_{s\to t}v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x))=v_{t}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\lim_{s\to t}v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x))=v_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">assuming continuity of <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and using that <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t,t}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t,t}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, using the parameterization</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">we find that</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\lim_{s\to t}\left\{(t-s)\partial_{t}v_{s,t}(x)+v_{s,t}(x)\right\}=v_{t,t}(x)=v_{t}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\lim_{s\to t}\left\{(t-s)\partial_{t}v_{s,t}(x)+v_{s,t}(x)\right\}=v_{t,t}(x)=v_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">This observation immediately leads to three “self-distillation” schemes, each of which proceeds by training the flow <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> on the diagonal <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=t</annotation></semantics></math> via flow matching, and simultaneously distilling it into a flow map by minimizing the square residual on one of the conditions in <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6</span></span><span id="Thmproposition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Euclidean self-distillation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al., 2025</a>)</cite>)<span id="Thmproposition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote a candidate flow map, and assume that <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous in both time arguments.
Moreover, let</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})=\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{t,t}(I_{t})-\partial_{t}{I}_{t}\right|^{2}\right]dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})=\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{t,t}(I_{t})-\partial_{t}{I}_{t}\right|^{2}\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">denote the flow matching loss on the diagonal <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the ideal flow map <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)=x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the unique minimizer over <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> of each of the following objective functions.</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Lagrangian self-distillation loss,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{t}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-v^{\theta}_{t,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖫𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{t}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-v^{\theta}_{t,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Eulerian self-distillation loss,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖤𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">iii.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The progressive self-distillation loss,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖯𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\gamma v^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})-(1-\gamma)v^{\theta}_{u,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t\mathrm{d}\gamma," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\gamma v^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})-(1-\gamma)v^{\theta}_{u,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t\mathrm{d}\gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(1-\gamma)s+\gamma t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(1-\gamma)s+\gamma t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For completeness, and for ease of the reader, we sketch the proof from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
We first observe that <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\partial_{t}{I}_{t}|I_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\partial_{t}{I}_{t}|I_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math> is the ideal flow.
From this, it follows that <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖫𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖤𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖯𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})\geq\mathcal{L}_{b}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, because the second term in each loss is non-negative.
Moreover, by <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the ideal flow map satisfies the Lagrangian equation <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Item i. ‣ Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> and the Eulerian equation <a href="#A1.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Item ii. ‣ Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, so that the second term is zero for both <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖫𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖤𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})</annotation></semantics></math> at the true flow map.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to show that the second loss in equation <a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Item iii. ‣ Proposition 6 (Euclidean self-distillation ( , )). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> imposes the semigroup condition.
To see this, we observe that we may write the semigroup condition as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="7" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{s,u}(x)+(t-u)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{s,u}(x)+(t-u)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff x+(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x+(u-s)v_{s,u}(x)+(t-u)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x+(u-s)v_{s,u}(x)+(t-u)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=((1-\gamma)s+\gamma t-s)v_{s,u}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=((1-\gamma)s+\gamma t-s)v_{s,u}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(t-(1-\gamma)s-\gamma t))v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(t-(1-\gamma)s-\gamma t))v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xe.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma(t-s)v_{s,u}(x)+(1-\gamma)(t-s)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma(t-s)v_{s,u}(x)+(1-\gamma)(t-s)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xf" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xf.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff v_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff v_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xf.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma v_{s,u}(x)+(1-\gamma)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma v_{s,u}(x)+(1-\gamma)v_{u,t}(X_{s,u}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">From the sequence of operations in equation <a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, we see that the second term in equation <a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Item iii. ‣ Proposition 6 (Euclidean self-distillation ( , )). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> penalises the square residual on a rescaled semigroup condition.
The minimiser therefore satisfies the semigroup condition, and by <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> is the ideal flow map.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stopgradients</span>.
In practice, it is beneficial, when optimising over neural networks, to use the <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> operator to control the flow of information.
This allows us to interpret the flow model <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}_{t,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}_{t,t}</annotation></semantics></math> as a “teacher”, which is used to provide a training signal for the map on the off diagonal <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the squared residuals presented in <a href="#Thmproposition6" title="Proposition 6 (Euclidean self-distillation ( , )). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> are minimized directly, gradients can align the trained flow model with the untrained flow map, rather than vice-versa.
To this end, we provide some concrete recommendations inspired by the setting when a frozen pre-trained teacher model is available.</p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For LSD, we recommend:</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{t}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}(v^{\theta}_{t,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖫𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{LSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{t}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}(v^{\theta}_{t,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For ESD, we recommend:</p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}(\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖤𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{ESD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}(\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s}))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For PSD, we recommend:</p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖯𝖲𝖣</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{PSD}}(\hat{v})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E32Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}(\gamma v^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})+(1-\gamma)v^{\theta}_{u,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t\mathrm{d}\gamma," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}(\gamma v^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})+(1-\gamma)v^{\theta}_{u,t}(X^{\theta}_{s,u}(I_{s})))\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t\mathrm{d}\gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(1-\gamma)s+\gamma t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(1-\gamma)s+\gamma t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">The recommendations in equation <a href="#A1.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> and equation <a href="#A1.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Item 3 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> are precisely what would arise given a pre-trained teacher.
The recommendation in equation <a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> is similar, but also places a <math id="A1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> on the spatial Jacobian of the model, which often improves optimization stability significantly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Flows and consistency training</span>.
Given the choice of <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in equation <a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, the resulting parameter gradient will be <span id="A1.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">linear</span> in <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}_{s,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}_{s,s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may then replace <math id="A1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> by the Monte Carlo estimate <math id="A1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}{I}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}{I}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> of the ideal flow <math id="A1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{s}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|I_{s}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{s}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|I_{s}=x]</annotation></semantics></math>, using the tower property of the conditional expectation <math id="A1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})\partial_{t}{I}_{s}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})\mathbb{E}\left[\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|I_{s}\right]\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})v_{s}(I_{s})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})\partial_{t}{I}_{s}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})\mathbb{E}\left[\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|I_{s}\right]\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[f(I_{s})v_{s}(I_{s})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> for any function <math id="A1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Without this choice of <math id="A1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>stopgrad</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}</annotation></semantics></math>, this replacement is not possible due to the quadratic term <math id="A1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|^{2}]\neq\mathbb{E}[|\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v_{s}(I_{s})|^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{t}{I}_{s}|^{2}]\neq\mathbb{E}[|\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v_{s}(I_{s})|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> because of the nonlinearity in <math id="A1.p10.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\cdot|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\cdot|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
With this <math id="A1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>stopgrad</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quadratic term is a constant from the perspective of the gradient and hence this discrepancy can be ignored.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p11.4" class="ltx_p">This trick is used by both consistency training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2023a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu &amp; Song, 2025</a>)</cite> and Mean Flows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>; in fact, these algorithms can be recovered by expanding</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{s}X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla X^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=I+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.5" class="ltx_p">Plugging equation <a href="#A1.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> into the Eulerian loss equation <a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}({\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}({\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}({\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex1Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.6" class="ltx_p">Replacing <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}_{s,s}(I_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> by the Monte Carlo estimate of the ideal flow as described above yields</p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(v^{\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(v^{\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(\partial_{s}{I}_{s}+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{s}{I}_{s}\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|-v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+(t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(\partial_{s}{I}_{s}+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{s}{I}_{s}\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.7" class="ltx_p">and then choosing to <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>stopgrad</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> term as well as the spatial gradient yields the Mean Flow/Consistency Training objective,</p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(v^{\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(v^{\theta})=\mathcal{L}_{b}(v^{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E35Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left((t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\partial_{s}{I}_{s}+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{s}{I}_{s}\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left((t-s)\partial_{s}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})+\partial_{s}{I}_{s}+(t-s)\nabla v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\partial_{s}{I}_{s}\right)\right|^{2}\right]\mathrm{d}s\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Generalised Flow Map Characterizations</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To show that the the propositions hold, let us first demonstrate the legality of the above claims, that the compared vectors indeed belong to the same tangent planes. For the semigroup condition, observe that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore is evidently coherent.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,t\in[0,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,t\in[0,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ B.1 Generalised Flow Map Characterizations ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that, for any <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,s,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,s,t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)=\exp_{x}((t-s)v_{s,t}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)=\exp_{x}((t-s)v_{s,t}(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, and, without loss of generality, suppose that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>. (The case <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;s</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly symmetric.) For <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the proof is trivial, as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{0}\in\mathcal{T}_{x}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{0}\in\mathcal{T}_{x}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}_{u}(x)\coloneqq X_{s,(1-s)u+s}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}_{u}(x)\coloneqq X_{s,(1-s)u+s}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which coincides with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-s)u+s=t\iff u=\frac{t-s}{1-s}=:\tilde{u}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-s)u+s=t\iff u=\frac{t-s}{1-s}=:\tilde{u}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Remarking that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((1-s)u+s)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((1-s)u+s)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a geodesic between <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}_{0}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}_{0}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}_{1}(x)=X_{s,1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}_{1}(x)=X_{s,1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=0\implies s=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=0\implies s=t</annotation></semantics></math>, from where the proof is also trivial. Therefore, it follows that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{u}\tilde{X}_{u}(x)=\log_{X_{s,u}(x)}(X_{s,1}(x))/(1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{u}\tilde{X}_{u}(x)=\log_{X_{s,u}(x)}(X_{s,1}(x))/(1-u)</annotation></semantics></math>, and considering the previous expression for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\tilde{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\tilde{u}</annotation></semantics></math> finalises the proof from the definition of the logarithmic map.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The above validates the Lagrangian condition. Let us also justify the Eulerian condition: by <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ B.1 Generalised Flow Map Characterizations ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x_{s})}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(x_{s})\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x_{s})}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let us now prove that <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t})_{x}[v_{s}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t})_{x}[v_{s}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math> is on the same tangent space.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t})_{x}[v_{s}(x)]\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t})_{x}[v_{s}(x)]\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ B.1 Generalised Flow Map Characterizations ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is true by definition. To see this, let <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M},\tau\mapsto\gamma(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M},\tau\mapsto\gamma(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> be a curve, such that <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)=x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}\gamma=v_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}\gamma=v_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. We therefore have that <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}\circ\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}\circ\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}(X_{s,t}\circ\gamma)(0)\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(\gamma(0))}\mathcal{M}=\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}(X_{s,t}\circ\gamma)(0)\in\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(\gamma(0))}\mathcal{M}=\mathcal{T}_{X_{s,t}(x)}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Knowing that <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{s,t})_{x}v_{s}(x)=\partial_{\tau}(X_{s,t}\circ\gamma)(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{s,t})_{x}v_{s}(x)=\partial_{\tau}(X_{s,t}\circ\gamma)(0)</annotation></semantics></math> concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove the main proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5 (Flow map characterization). ‣ Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us first prove the Lagrangian condition. It comes naturally as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(x_{s})=x_{t}\implies\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=\partial_{t}x_{t}=v_{t}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(x_{s})=x_{t}\implies\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=\partial_{t}x_{t}=v_{t}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is true by definition, since <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t})_{t\in[0,1]}</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution of <a href="#S3.EGx2" title="3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. As for the Eulerian condition, we note too that, for any <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))=x</annotation></semantics></math>. (So, it is also invertible.) Taking the derivative through <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))=\partial_{s}x" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))=\partial_{s}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))+(\mathrm{d}X_{s,t})_{X_{t,s}(x)}[\partial_{s}X_{t,s}(x)]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(X_{t,s}(x))+(\mathrm{d}X_{s,t})_{X_{t,s}(x)}[\partial_{s}X_{t,s}(x)]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line is due to the chain rule on manifolds. Moreover, by the probability flow ODE, we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}X_{t,s}(x)=v_{s}(X_{t,s}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}X_{t,s}(x)=v_{s}(X_{t,s}(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, and, letting <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=X_{t,s}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=X_{t,s}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(y)+(\mathrm{d}X_{s,t})_{y}[v_{s}(y)]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}X_{s,t}(y)+(\mathrm{d}X_{s,t})_{y}[v_{s}(y)]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible for any <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and defined on <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is bijective, and thus we can freely rename <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to conclude that the Eulerian condition holds. Finally, the semigroup condition is trivially true from the definition: <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{u,t}\circ X_{s,u})(x_{s})=x_{t}=X_{s,t}(x_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{u,t}\circ X_{s,u})(x_{s})=x_{t}=X_{s,t}(x_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof for <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
This property follows from the Lagrangian condition. We have that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the limit on both sides, we find that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=\lim_{s\to t}v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=\lim_{s\to t}v_{t}(X_{s,t}(x_{s}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=v_{t}\left(\lim_{s\to t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})\right)=v_{t}(x_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})=v_{t}\left(\lim_{s\to t}X_{s,t}(x_{s})\right)=v_{t}(x_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line comes from the continuity of the limit.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)\in[0,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=v_{t,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{s\to t}\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=v_{t,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following elementary Riemannian geometry, we find that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\partial_{t}\exp_{x}((t-s)v_{s,t}(x))=\mathrm{d}(\exp_{x})_{(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)}(v_{s,t}(x)+(t-s)\partial_{t}v_{s,t}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}X_{s,t}(x)=\partial_{t}\exp_{x}((t-s)v_{s,t}(x))=\mathrm{d}(\exp_{x})_{(t-s)v_{s,t}(x)}(v_{s,t}(x)+(t-s)\partial_{t}v_{s,t}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Knowing that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}(\exp_{x})_{\vec{0}}=\mathrm{Id}_{\mathcal{T}_{x}\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}(\exp_{x})_{\vec{0}}=\mathrm{Id}_{\mathcal{T}_{x}\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and taking the limit, we find the desired conclusion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Generalised Self-Distillation Losses</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.2 Generalised Self-Distillation losses ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The loss is zero if and only if <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}X_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s})=v_{t,t}^{\theta}(X_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}X_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s})=v_{t,t}^{\theta}(X_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s}))</annotation></semantics></math> almost everywhere. We can conclude by <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS3.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS3.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Generalised Self-Distillation losses ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The loss is zero if and only if <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s,t}^{\theta}(x_{s})-\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t}^{\theta})_{x_{s}}[v_{s}^{\theta}(x_{s})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s,t}^{\theta}(x_{s})-\mathrm{d}(X_{s,t}^{\theta})_{x_{s}}[v_{s}^{\theta}(x_{s})]=0</annotation></semantics></math> almost everywhere. We can conclude by <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A2.SS3.p5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.SS3.p5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 3.2 Generalised Self-Distillation losses ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The loss is zero if and only if <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{u,t}^{\theta}(X_{s,u}^{\theta}(x))=X_{s,t}^{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{u,t}^{\theta}(X_{s,u}^{\theta}(x))=X_{s,t}^{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> almost everywhere. We can conclude by <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Generalised Flow Maps ‣ 3 Method ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Connections to existing methods</h3>

<section id="A2.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.1 </span>Generalised Mean Flows</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generalising Mean Flows directly is non-trivial as it requires defining the integral of a vector field on a manifold properly, which would involve parallel transport and therefore derivatives thereof. Also, Mean Flows operate on the vector field level as opposed to Flow Map Matching which operates on the level of the flow map. It is difficult to go from one level to another directly, as it will involve non-trivial curvature terms. Instead, we propose to heuristically follow our derivations in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Self-Distillation on Euclidean spaces ‣ Generalised Flow Maps for Few-Step Generative Modelling on Riemannian Manifolds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, in the “stopgradients” section. Indeed, we can see that our loss involves the instantaneous vector field of the modelled flow map, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}_{t,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}_{t,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, as opposed to the ideal flow <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the use of the Levi-Civita connection along <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{s}(I_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{s}(I_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> instead of the differential evaluated at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{s,s}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{s,s}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{G\text{-}MF}}({\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{t,s,(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\left\lVert v_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(\partial_{s}I_{s}-(t-s)\nabla_{v_{s}(I_{s})}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\right)\right\rVert_{g}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>MF</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{G\text{-}MF}}({\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{t,s,(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\left\lVert v_{s,t}^{\theta}(I_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(\partial_{s}I_{s}-(t-s)\nabla_{v_{s}(I_{s})}v^{\theta}_{s,t}(I_{s})\right)\right\rVert_{g}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which indeed recovers the Euclidean case as a special case. The Levi-Civita connection, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla:\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})\times\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})\to\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">∇</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>𝔛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔛</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla:\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})\times\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})\to\mathfrak{X}(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,X)\mapsto\nabla_{v}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,X)\mapsto\nabla_{v}X</annotation></semantics></math>, is the unique torsion-free, bilinear, metric compatible connection on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{M},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{M},g)</annotation></semantics></math> that respects the Leibniz rule in <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and it defines a notion of covariant derivative for the vector fields on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{M},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{M},g)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.2 </span>Generalised Shortcut Models</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Shortcut models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Frans et al., 2025</a>)</cite> are exactly trained to enforce the semigroup property but on a discrete time grid. Expressed in our notation, the loss amounts to</p>
<table id="A2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)={\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)+\mathbb{E}_{s,d,(x_{0},x_{1})}\left\lVert v_{s,s+2d}(x_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(v_{s+d,s+2d}(x_{s}+dv_{s,s+d}(x_{s})\right)\right\rVert_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FM</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)={\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)+\mathbb{E}_{s,d,(x_{0},x_{1})}\left\lVert v_{s,s+2d}(x_{s})-\mathrm{stopgrad}\left(v_{s+d,s+2d}(x_{s}+dv_{s,s+d}(x_{s})\right)\right\rVert_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> can be seen as the time difference <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-s</annotation></semantics></math>, and, letting <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> be uniformly distributed, we recover exactly Euclidean Progressive self-distillation, as noted in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boffi et al. (2024)</a></cite>. The Riemannian case is strictly analogous, where the + operation is replaced by the exponential map, and the appropriate manifold distance is used.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Empirical MMD calculation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any distributions <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> with support <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{M},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{M},g)</annotation></semantics></math>, and with respective independent samples <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i})_{1\leq i\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i})_{1\leq i\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i})_{1\leq i\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i})_{1\leq i\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{MMD}}(p,q)\coloneqq\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(p_{i},p_{j})\right)+\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(q_{i},q_{j})\right)-2\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(p_{i},q_{j})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>MMD</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{MMD}}(p,q)\coloneqq\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(p_{i},p_{j})\right)+\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(q_{i},q_{j})\right)-2\exp\left(-\kappa d_{g}^{2}(p_{i},q_{j})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We choose <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to be equal to the size of the test set.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Additional results</h3>

<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Plots of densities for the various datasets and all compared methods. Depicted in red are the test-set samples. Datasets from left to right: volcano, earthquake, flood, fire.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.F7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:183.4pt;vertical-align:-89.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-15.3pt,7.1pt) scale(0.928374343734681,0.928374343734681) ;">
<table id="A3.F7.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
